{
  "summary": "Whip is a React Native (Expo SDK 57) + Rust mobile client for a remote Herdr server. It never runs Herdr locally; the device connects to the host over SSH (Russh), reaches Herdr's local API sockets via SSH stream-local channels, and renders Herdr's server-owned state as native screens. One shared Rust core (`whip-ssh` static lib + WhipSsh TurboModule) backs both iOS and Android. Chat View reads Codex/OpenCode agent transcripts over the same SSH connection (never from terminal pixels). Strong security posture: strict host-key verification, platform credential stores, QR-based one-shot pubkey enrollment (WP4/whipair) using only the existing SSH port.",
  "architecture": "Three planes: (1) Transport — device→host SSH via russh, optionally through nested OSSH jump hosts; `whip-ssh` loads one process-wide known_hosts repo, returns typed unknown/changed fingerprint challenges. (2) Control — Rust AppCore + one HostRuntime per host; HostRuntime owns an Arc<HerdrConnection> as sole owner of the authenticated SshSession + generation. It opens SSH stream-local channels to Herdr's local API socket: short-lived request channels for structured actions/snapshots (Herdr 'Unix API accepts one request then closes'), plus a persistent subscription channel for events (JSONL framing, subscription_started ack, in-flight replay). (3) Terminal — each pane opens an independent stream-local channel to the client-protocol socket: Hello/Welcome/AttachTerminal state machine, binary length-prefixed ANSI frames over UniFFI/JSI (no JSON on hot path); xterm WebView renders ANSI. Rust owns all Herdr JSON; React Native gets typed versioned projections and sends semantic operations. Ping→pong handshake reads Herdr version/protocol (accepts protocols 17–22).",
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "ARCHITECTURE.md",
      "description": "Three-plane architecture: transport/control/terminal; AppCore vs HostRuntime state ownership; host-key, protocol, terminal, transcript details"
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "description": "Product intro; iOS/Android install; how-it-works, performance latencies, Chat View, offline fallback; architecture pointer"
    },
    {
      "path": "PRIVACY.md",
      "description": "On-device data, credential storage (Keystore/Keychain + Android Block Store recovery), local notifications/speech, no telemetry"
    },
    {
      "path": "whipair/README.md",
      "description": "WP4 QR pairing protocol: one-shot Ed25519 restricted credential, host-key pin, forced-command exchange, verification code"
    }
  ],
  "report": "Answers to the 7 questions (paths cited):\n\n**1. Rust core (packages/react-native-whip-ssh/rust):** Does the SSH transport (russh) + Herdr protocol client. AppCore (application/session state) and per-host HostRuntime (authoritative HostState, reconnect, terminal registry, agent transcripts, SFTP/Git/forwards). RN talks to it via one WhipSsh TurboModule (New Architecture) exposing semantic operations; receives typed binary frames + versioned projections. No Herdr JSON crosses the RN boundary; Rust alone parses it.\n\n**2. Herdr surface:** NOT the human 'terminal attach' CLI. Whip opens SSH stream-local channels DIRECTLY to Herdr's Unix API socket (short-lived request channels) + a persistent subscription channel for events, and per-pane client-protocol socket for terminals (ARCHITECTURE terminal plane). Workspaces/tabs/panes via structured socket API — create/focus/rename/split/resize/send/close/launch. 'TerminalAttach' bypasses Herdr's management prefix router, so Whip exposes ws/tab/pane ops as native actions (ARCHITECTURE).\n\n**3. Chat View:** Rust HostRuntime uses the pane's Herdr `agent_session` ID to (a) OpenCode — cold snapshot via official `opencode export`, then poll newer durable events via `opencode db` (validates sequence continuity, falls back to export on divergence); (b) Codex — resolves rollout matching Herdr's native session ID, reads initial JSONL snapshot, follows appended records. All over the SAME authenticated SSH connection (no relay); normalized into typed AgentTranscript (messages, thinking, tools, diffs). Composer text goes back to the same Herdr pane/PTY.\n\n**4. Offline:** Read-only 'virtual Herdr backend' — Whip periodically caches bounded recent ANSI per visible terminal in memory; when transport connecting/disconnected/error, a local virtual backend owns that transcript + per-terminal logical scroll position and presents it read-only (no local Herdr/agent). Per-terminal NATIVE COMPOSER outbox: messages queue in memory, retried in order on reconnect. Both are session fallbacks — do not survive app restart (README 'How it works').\n\n**5. WP4/whipair pairing:** `whipair` host-side tool creates a temporary Ed25519 key, adds only its public half to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys with `restrict,command=\"whipair exchange --socket …\"` (disables shell/PTY/forwarding; forced command accepts one JSON EnrollmentRequest on stdin, relays via Unix socket to visible whipair). QR = `WP4:` + Base45 binary: address type+SSH host, port, username, temp Ed25519 seed, SSH host-key SHA-256 pin. Phone sends enrollment data ONLY after verifying host key vs QR digest; six-digit verification code shown on both; user approves; host appends permanent key idempotently/atomically, replies EnrollmentResponse, removes temp entry. No new port/relay.\n\n**6. Notifications/speech:** Blocked/done notifications, vibration, optional speech are all produced ON-DEVICE (local only, PRIVACY.md). Configurable alert duration; dismissed by returning to app; speech audible locally.\n\n**7. iOS unsigned:** CI compiles a thin unsigned device app → uploads `whip-ios-unsigned-compile-only.app.zip` as a short-lived GitHub Actions artifact — compile validation ONLY: not attached to releases, not on App Store/TestFlight, unsigned, not directly installable. iOS 16.4+/ARM64. For a device build, use Xcode signed build (`ios/HerdR.xcworkspace`, scripts/install-ios-device.sh); iOS-simulator EAS profile is unsigned. Signed iOS beta/release is listed as an upcoming milestone (ARCHITECTURE 'Current transport/product milestones').\n\nInferences: '[INFERENCE] whip-ssh crate path' derived from packages/react-native-whip-ssh name given in README."
}

