    },
    {
      "path": "CONTEXT.md",
      "description": "Glossary pinning Host/Jump Host/Pairing/Agent/Composer/Attach/Shell Terminal/Row Layout/Notification terms."
    },
    {
      "path": "Sources/Heeler/Transport/",
      "description": "Transport layer: HerdrWire.swift, JSONValue.swift, EventsSession.swift, HerdrEvents.swift, HeelerSSHTransport.swift, DeviceKey*.swift, HostKey*.swift."
    },
    {
      "path": "Sources/Heeler/Console/",
      "description": "Console UI: AgentCardView, AgentRowLayout, AgentArgumentsField, AgentName, AgentComposerStore/View, AgentControlKeyboard, AgentDirectInput*."
    },
    {
      "path": "relay/",
      "description": "Cloudflare Workers stateless push relay: POST /push, APNs JWT signing, rate limits."
    }
  ],
  "architecture": "Five Swift targets: Heeler (app: Console, Transport, Terminal, Composer/Attachments/Skills/Snippets, Notifications, LiveActivities, Pairing, Hosts), HeelerActivityCore + HeelerWidgets (Live Activity widget), HeelerNotificationCore + HeelerNotificationService (APNs decrypt extension), plus Packages/HeelerSSH (libssh2+OpenSSL XCFrameworks) and a Node herdr plugin (plugin/) + a Cloudflare-Workers relay (relay/). Transport layer: libssh2 direct-streamlocal channels onto herdr.sock for JSON-RPC, a reserved Events channel for events.subscribe, one reserved Attach PTY; 8+1 forwarding budget, 8+1 session budget under OpenSSH MaxSessions default 10. All herdr JSON shapes decoded via JSONValue.swift/HerdrWire.swift; UI consumes Transport abstraction. Plugin drives pairing enrollment + notifications/live-activity hooks (pane.agent_status_changed, [[events]]), and exports the herdr sidebar layout (sidebar.json).",
  "report": "## Heeler iOS app internals (github.com/ZingerLittleBee/Heeler, Apache-2.0, Swift 6)\nSources: AGENTS.md (→CLAUDE.md), CONTEXT.md (336 lines), PRIVACY.md, plugin/README.md (546 lines), docs/adr/0001-0016, docs/guides/vps-jump-host.md, docs/agents/live-activity-contract.md, relay/README, CHANGELOG.md. Evidence paths are repo-relative; [INFERENCE] marks claims not stated verbatim.\n\n### 1. Transport (ADR-0002 superseded by ADR-0011; README 'How it connects')\n- History: v1 used exec + socat (ADR-0002): per-request `socat - UNIX-CONNECT:<sock>` exec channels + one long-lived channel for `events.subscribe`; `exec herdr agent attach <pane>` bootstrap line in a PTY shell. Required socat on every host.\n- Current (ADR-0011 accepted): repository-local `Packages/HeelerSSH` wrapping libssh2 + OpenSSL (checked-in XCFrameworks). Each herdr request opens a `direct-streamlocal` channel onto the herdr Unix socket (`herdr.sock`); one long-lived reserved channel carries the event stream; interactive terminals run `herdr agent attach --takeover` on an SSH PTY. Direct connections use non-blocking POSIX sockets (DispatchSourceRead/Write); nested Jump Host sessions use an internal byte transport over an outer `direct-tcpip` channel. Every SSH hop has one non-blocking session driver that serializes all `LIBSSH2_SESSION` calls.\n- herdr JSON API is NDJSON over a Unix domain socket, ONE REQUEST PER CONNECTION, so each RPC opens its own direct-streamlocal channel (bounded by forwarding-budget queue, 8 ordinary RPC + 1 reserved events; 8 exec/SFTP + 1 reserved Attach in the session budget). `agent.prompt` (no `wait`) returns immediately as delivery acknowledgment; `wait` variant was rejected (occupies an RPC channel for an agent turn).\n- Events stream: `events.subscribe` on a dedicated channel — real-time while foregrounded; herdr replays NO state on subscribe (ADR-0011/0012), so Agent Inventory is replaced wholesale on each snapshot. `pane.agent_status_changed` is the precise, tiny, usable push signal; `pane_output_changed` isn't subscribable and `pane.output_matched` is edge-triggered (ADR-0012) — rejected as a refresh signal. herdr `ping` is the authoritative health check (exercises SSH, both jumps, streamlocal, socket, server).\n- Takeover/PTY: `herdr agent attach` resolves an Agent over the API to its terminal_id and calls `run_terminal_attach` (per herdr v0.8.2 source, ADR-0015). `terminal attach` targets a terminal ID via the client socket (`herdr.sock`→`herdr-client.sock`, server/socket_paths.rs); supports raw input, resize, and `--takeover`. One writable attach owner per terminal; a second attach without --takeover is refused; takeover displaces the prior owner with an explicit shutdown message. Missing terminal fails outright (no hang). Unix-only.\n- Stream-local failure classification: libssh2 can't distinguish stale socket vs forwarding-policy denial; Heeler runs one read-only remote `test -S` diagnostic. Socket missing → socketNotFound; socket exists → one honest combined 'herdr not running OR streamlocal disabled' failure, deliberately NOT retryable (user must fix).\n- Attach Link: web URLs observed in terminal during a detail session are collected and remain available until leaving detail (CONTEXT.md; ADR-0010).\n\n### 2. Console data model (ADR-0012/0013; plugin sidebar snapshot v1; CONTEXT.md)\n- Agents across Hosts rendered as a flat list or by-Host grouped list with collapsible sections, sorted Blocked-first, filterable by Host, searchable. Per-agent model (`AgentInfo`/`ConsoleAgent`, files under Sources/Heeler/Console/: AgentCardView, AgentRowLayout, AgentArgumentsField, AgentName).\n- herdr JSON fields driving the agent list: `pane_id`, `workspace_id`, `agent` (kind: claude/codex/...), `display_agent`/`name`, `agent_status` (idle/working/blocked/done/unknown), `terminal_id`, `cwd`, `terminal_title`/`terminal_title_stripped`, `state_icon`/`state_text` (sidebar tokens), `rows_by_agent` per-kind layout overrides, workspace label via `workspace list`. Agent Status (Blocked) drives sort order + notifications. State icon appears as the Row-1 status badge, never a field.\n- Agent Row Layout: 3 fixed Row Slots per Host; Rows 1-2 come from the Host's herdr sidebar layout (plugin snapshot `sidebar.json`, ADR plugin 0.4.0), Row 3 is Heeler's. herdr per-kind `rows_by_agent` overrides are decoded but not applied. Order: user-saved layout > plugin snapshot > Heeler default; never merged. Sync-from-plugin refills Rows 1-2.\n- 'New Agent' can start in an existing Workspace, a new Worktree of one, or a new Workspace at a remote directory; uses `tab.create` (workspace_id + concrete cwd + focus:false, ADR-0015) and create-agent APIs. There IS an Agent switcher (shared by detail surfaces) at the bottom of the Composer — so yes, there is pane/agent switching UI; workspaces/worktrees are launch targets, not a browse-list surface. Agent Inventory readiness modeled separately (unknown vs loading vs empty).\n\n### 3. Composer internals (ADR-0012 superseded by ADR-0013; ADR-0009, 0016)\n- Composer is the DEFAULT authored input on Agent detail: a native draft field that composes fully on-device (iOS keyboard with autocorrect/IME/dictation) and delivers in ONE piece via one `agent.prompt` request (without `wait`) — no remote-echo latency while drafting, no keystroke round-trips. When Agent Status is Blocked, Send inserts the draft into the Attach PTY without Enter (herdr 0.8.2 rejects `agent.prompt` while blocked because auto-Enter would confirm/dismiss a dialog); the tools keyboard submits (Enter) or cancels (Esc).\n- Direct Input (ADR-0016): opt-in app-wide preference, default off; hides Composer, routes the iOS keyboard + a compact app-owned shortcut row (Esc/Tab/Shift-Tab/Enter) into the live Attach PTY; Skills/Snippets still insert into the draft/pane without Enter.\n- Tools keyboard: tabbed pad with large Agent controls (Esc/Tab/Shift-Tab/arrows/Enter/Backspace → directly to PTY) and a full Terminal keyboard (characters, Ctrl/Alt/Shift, fn keys) via libghostty `UITerminalView.sendKey`; Skills and Snippets panels only insert text into the draft (ADR-0009 insert-without-submit).\n- Skills (Sources/Heeler/Skills/) and Snippets (Snippets/) insert into the Composer draft and nothing more; the user still delivers. Skills are herdr agent skills surfaced in the tools pad; Snippets are a global user set, optional Title, multiline wrapped in bracketed paste (`ESC[200~...ESC[201~`) when the app tracked DECSET 2004.\n- Attachments (ADR-0006): Add stages one image (decoded/bounded/metadata-stripped) or file (≤64 MiB, random local name, safe extension kept) over SFTP to private Host temp dirs (atomic completion); the resulting Host path is copied to an expiring local clipboard (24h) and appended to the draft with a trailing space — never auto-submitted. Completed Host files outlive the screen (ADR-0005).\n- libghostty (ADR-0004): `InMemoryTerminalSession` — PTY bytes in via `receive(_:)`, Ghostty write/resize callbacks feed Attach transport. Heeler owns two-mode keyboard, touch-scroll routing (normal-buffer → scrollback actions; alternate-screen → SGR/legacy wheel encoding via a tracked DEC private-mode tracker), native text-selection sheet, URL policy, and pinch zoom (Ghostty's own pinch disabled; app routes through TerminalController persisted size). Ghostty's fixterms encoding preserves Ctrl-I/Tab vs Ctrl-M/Enter distinctions.\n\n### 4. E2E-encrypted push + Live Activities (ADR-0008, ADR-0014, PRIVACY.md, plugin README, live-activity-contract.md)\n- Pipeline: herdr plugin `[[events]]` hooks on `pane.agent_status_changed` run short-lived Node scripts (notify-hook.js for alerts; activity-hook.js for Live Activity). Notify hook debounces (~5s, re-checks status via `herdr agent get <pane>`), dedupes, and for eligible devices POSTs to the relay. herdr runs BOTH hooks per event (verified 0.8.0).\n- Push Relay (https://heeler-apns.bybee.dev, Cloudflare Workers, stateless): holds the APNs `.p8`, signs ES256 JWT, forwards to Apple. No accounts/db/queues/durable storage; device tokens + ciphertext + source IP + timing pass through in volatile per-instance memory with 1-minute rate limits. Cannot read content (never receives the Notification Key). Custom relay URL supported for self-built apps; must use APNs creds for that bundle ID.\n- End-to-end encryption: per-Host symmetric Notification Key generated on device, stored in shared Keychain (AfterFirstUnlock; mirrored in shared container protected-until-first-unlock, backup-excluded), copied to the Host in `notifications.json` (plugin config dir via `herdr plugin config-dir`). Envelope `{v:1, kid, n, ct}` — AES-256-GCM, 12-byte nonce, AAD `HERDR-NOTIFY:1`, kid = first 8 bytes of SHA-256(key). App's Notification Service Extension decrypts; untrusted/corrupt → generic fallback banner.\n- Notification Registration: app writes push token + Notification Key over SSH; per host, repeatable, independent of pairing. Devices fan out edge-side (one entry per token). `410 Unregistered` → plugin prunes dead token.\n- Triggers: Blocked + Done (Done individually toggleable; Working/Idle never alert). Foreground: system push banners silenced, in-app banner driven off the app's own live event stream (near-zero latency, mirrors plugin gates).\n- Live Activities (ADR-0014): one per Host. App starts locally (`pushType:.token`) and writes per-activity token + `pinned_pane_ids` + resolved `row_layout` + `host_name` into registration file; after suspension the plugin activity-hook lists agents (`herdr agent list`), resolves workspace labels, coalesces (1.5s latest-wins claim + unchanged suppression), and posts update/end. HYBRID content-state: plaintext counts {working,blocked,done} + encrypted details envelope (AAD `HERDR-ACTIVITY:1`, agents[] with kind/name/pane/status/title/workspace/rows, capped at 5 visible) decrypted at render time by the widget from shared Keychain. Counts + update/end/priority/timestamp are cleartext to the relay (relayed to APNs) because Live Activity pushes have no service-extension hook and the system must decode content-state; per-agent identity stays encrypted. Statuses: working/blocked/done shown, idle/unknown hidden. Priority 5 default, 10 only for a newly-blocked agent. No push-to-start in v1 (killed app ~50% success; new working agent while app dead isn't seen until next run). AgentActivityAttributes name is shipped forever (APNs attributes-type). Live Activity shows counts + pinned rows; Dynamic Island compact = counts.\n\n### 5. QR pairing (ADR-0007; plugin README)\n- `herdr plugin install ZingerLittleBee/Heeler/plugin --ref main --yes`, then `herdr plugin action invoke heeler.pair` renders a QR in a herdr popup pane. Envelope: `HERDR-PAIR:<version>:<base64url(JSON)>`.\n- Payload v1: `addrs` (candidate addresses in try order), `port` (fixed at 22 currently — known limitation), `user`, `fp` (host key fingerprint `SHA256:`+43 unpadded base64, pinned instead of TOFU), optional `seed` (raw 32-byte Bootstrap Key Ed25519 seed) + `exp` (Unix-seconds TTL). No seed/exp = config-only code. Decoders ignore unknown fields; canonical encoding asserted by shared test vectors.\n- Bootstrap Key lifecycle: ephemeral Ed25519 generated on the Host, single-use, 2-minute TTL; public half written to `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` as a restricted line `restrict,command=\"'<node>' '<plugin>/src/pair-accept.js' ... --pairing-id <id>\"` with comment `herdr-pairing:<id>:exp:<unix>`. The forced command performs Enrollment only. Removed on success (self-revoke), TTL expiry, popup exit, or a sweep of expired lines at next start. Pending state in `$HERDR_PLUGIN_STATE_DIR/pending/`, never the checkout.\n- Enrollment: app connects with Bootstrap Key (raw seed), writes its Device Key public line + newline to stdin; server answers `HERDR-ENROLL:OK:<SHA256:fp>` (appended/authored, bootstrap revoked, exit 0) or typed ERR lines (invalid_key, no_input, expired, unknown_pairing). Then app reconnects with the Device Key. Host persisted only after the full ceremony.\n- App: Device Key = Ed25519 keypair generated on-device, private half stays in Keychain; public half is what a Host authorizes. Pairing uses a dedicated one-shot client beside Transport. Fallbacks: manual Host form + copy-paste authorized_keys line. Risk accepted: same-room attacker photographing the QR and racing within TTL. Reachability scoped to same-LAN/same-VPN; cellular-only phones unsupported.\n\n### 6. libghostty terminal + takeover + SFTP attachments\n- libghostty-spm (ADR-0004): UIKit `UITerminalView` + `InMemoryTerminalSession`; owns parsing, Metal rendering, CoreText, IME, scrollback. Heeler owns keyboards, touch-scroll routing, selection sheet, URL policy, Attach lifecycle. Pinched version; verify SwiftPM checksum before updates. Uses `sendKey` API (libghostty-spm ≥1.6.20260909). ~30 themes, JetBrains Mono & IBM Plex Mono bundled, pinch zoom app-owned.\n- Takeover semantics (ADR-0015): Shell Terminal (Open Terminal) creates a fresh herdr tab via `tab.create` in the Agent's cwd (then worktree path), then attaches the returned root pane's shell through `herdr terminal attach <terminal_id> --takeover` on the existing SSH PTY pipeline. Takeover is safe because the tab is freshly minted; the flow never targets an arbitrary existing terminal (would displace a desktop attach owner). Back detaches, leaving the remote tab alive for desktop handoff. Agent Attach `--takeover` similarly displaces a stale terminal owner. One Host terminal lifetime: opening Shell Terminal tears Agent Attach down first; leaving lets it rejoin.\n- Attachments over SFTP (ADR-0006): Transport.stageImage/stageFile share one SFTP impl (private Host tmp dirs, restrictive perms, partial-file compensation, atomic completion, shared session-channel budget). ≤64 MiB files; images re-encoded metadata-stripped. No PTY binary injection (terminal input has no file framing).\n\n### 7. Worktrees, jump hosts, rough edges\n- Worktrees (CONTEXT.md): a fresh `git checkout` of a workspace's repo created by herdr as its own workspace; branch defaults to herdr's generated `worktree/<name>` off HEAD; removing the Worktree deletes the checkout and closes its workspace but the branch survives. Snapshot worktree metadata describes the main checkout; only `is_linked_worktree` makes a workspace eligible for linked-Worktree removal. New Agent can start in a new Worktree.\n- Jump Hosts (docs/guides/vps-jump-host.md + vps-jump-host-setup.md): reach unroutable Macs behind NAT via a restricted VPS. Mac makes a persistent outbound reverse-SSH tunnel (launchd) publishing a loopback-only port (e.g. 127.0.0.1:2222); iOS connects to the VPS (herdr-jump account, direct-tcpip to 127.0.0.1:2222 only, `AllowTcpForwarding local`, `PermitOpen 127.0.0.1:2222`, `MaxSessions 0`), then does a SECOND SSH handshake to the Mac. Keys verified at both hops; Device Key authorized on both the VPS jump account and the Mac. VPS can observe metadata/interrupt but not passively read the inner session while host keys are verified. No stream-local over the jump; nested driver uses outer direct-tcpip as transport.\n- Rough edges / limitations (documented): requires Node ≥20 + herdr ≥0.7.5 + OpenSSH with stream-local forwarding enabled (onboarding calls out when disabled); advertised SSH port fixed at 22 (plugin README known limitation); herdr API wire shapes carry no stability guarantee (hooks parse leniently); no push-to-start for Live Activities; Live Activity widget shows counts-only on watch/pre-first-unlock; remote history NOT addressable (`pane.read` visible/recent + 1000-line cap, no offset) so no server-side scroll history; shell tabs not projected into Console and outside notification routing; Agent Attach is display-only under Composer (dual-prompt collision); relay is a single point of failure for notifications only (Console/Attach never touch it); App Store availability limited by country; personal-use emphasis 'expect rough edges'. [INFERENCE: no separate 'sync' beyond the sidebar-layout plugin export; no multi-account server.]"
}

