  "summary": "Heeler is a native SwiftUI iOS 18+ agent console for herdr that talks the herdr JSON API over SSH. Transport is libssh2 (Packages/HeelerSSH, replacing Citadel/NIOSSH per ADR-0011): each request opens a direct-streamlocal channel to the herdr Unix socket (herdr.sock), one long-lived channel carries events.subscribe (NDJSON event stream), and interactive terminals run 'herdr agent attach --takeover' on an SSH PTY (ADR-0015 'herdr terminal attach <id> --takeover' for shells). UI goes through a Transport adapter, never SSH directly. Core features: status-sorted Agent Console (Blocked first), libghostty-rendered live terminal with native scrollback/selection, a local native Composer (drafts on-device, delivers via one agent.prompt request — no keystroke echo latency), Skills/Snippets that only insert into the draft, SFTP attachment staging (≤64 MiB), QR pairing via herdr plugin 'heeler.pair' (single-use 2-min Bootstrap Key + forced-command enrollment), end-to-end AES-256-GCM encrypted APNs push notifications + Live Activities through a stateless developer-hosted Push Relay (https://heeler-apns.bybee.dev, Cloudflare Workers), Worktrees, and SSH Jump Hosts. Private key stays in iOS Keychain; no accounts/analytics; custom relay URL supported for self-built apps.",
