  "report": "## Heeler iOS app internals (github.com/ZingerLittleBee/Heeler, Apache-2.0, Swift 6)\nSources: AGENTS.md (→CLAUDE.md), CONTEXT.md (336 lines), PRIVACY.md, plugin/README.md (546 lines), docs/adr/0001-0016, docs/guides/vps-jump-host.md, docs/agents/live-activity-contract.md, relay/README, CHANGELOG.md. Evidence paths are repo-relative; [INFERENCE] marks claims not stated verbatim.\n\n### 1. Transport (ADR-0002 superseded by ADR-0011; README 'How it connects')\n- History: v1 used exec + socat (ADR-0002): per-request `socat - UNIX-CONNECT:<sock>` exec channels + one long-lived channel for `events.subscribe`; `exec herdr agent attach <pane>` bootstrap line in a PTY shell. Required socat on every host.\n- Current (ADR-0011 accepted): repository-local `Packages/HeelerSSH` wrapping libssh2 + OpenSSL (checked-in XCFrameworks). Each herdr request opens a `direct-streamlocal` channel onto the herdr Unix socket (`herdr.sock`); one long-lived reserved channel carries the event stream; interactive terminals run `herdr agent attach --takeover` on an SSH PTY. Direct connections use non-blocking POSIX sockets (DispatchSourceRead/Write); nested Jump Host sessions use an internal byte transport over an outer `direct-tcpip` channel. Every SSH hop has one non-blocking session driver that serializes all `LIBSSH2_SESSION` calls.\n- herdr JSON API is NDJSON over a Unix domain socket, ONE REQUEST PER CONNECTION, so each RPC opens its own direct-streamlocal channel (bounded by forwarding-budget queue, 8 ordinary RPC + 1 reserved events; 8 exec/SFTP + 1 reserved Attach in the session budget). `agent.prompt` (no `wait`) returns immediately as delivery acknowledgment; `wait` variant was rejected (occupies an RPC channel for an agent turn).\n- Events stream: `events.subscribe` on a dedicated channel — real-time while foregrounded; herdr replays NO state on subscribe (ADR-0011/0012), so Agent Inventory is replaced wholesale on each snapshot. `pane.agent_status_changed` is the precise