 cleartext to the relay (relayed to APNs) because Live Activity pushes have no service-extension hook and the system must decode content-state; per-agent identity stays encrypted. Statuses: working/blocked/done shown, idle/unknown hidden. Priority 5 default, 10 only for a newly-blocked agent. No push-to-start in v1 (killed app ~50% success; new working agent while app dead isn't seen until next run). AgentActivityAttributes name is shipped forever (APNs attributes-type). Live Activity shows counts + pinned rows; Dynamic Island compact = counts.\n\n### 5. QR pairing (ADR-0007; plugin README)\n- `herdr plugin install ZingerLittleBee/Heeler/plugin --ref main --yes`, then `herdr plugin action invoke heeler.pair` renders a QR in a herdr popup pane. Envelope: `HERDR-PAIR:<version>:<base64url(JSON)>`.\n- Payload v1: `addrs` (candidate addresses in try order), `port` (fixed at 22 currently — known limitation), `user`, `fp` (host key fingerprint `SHA256:`+43 unpadded base64, pinned instead of TOFU), optional `seed` (raw 32-byte Bootstrap Key Ed25519 seed) + `exp` (Unix-seconds TTL). No seed/exp = config-only code. Decoders ignore unknown fields; canonical encoding asserted by shared test vectors.\n- Bootstrap Key lifecycle: ephemeral Ed25519 generated on the Host, single-use, 2-minute TTL; public half written to `~/.ssh/authorized_keys` as a restricted line `restrict,command=\"'<node>' '<plugin>/src/pair-accept.js' ... --pairing-id <id>\"` with comment `herdr-pairing:<id>:exp:<unix>`. The forced command performs Enrollment only. Removed on success (self-revoke), TTL expiry, popup exit, or a sweep of expired lines at next start. Pending state in `$HERDR_PLUGIN_STATE_DIR/pending/`, never the checkout.\n- Enrollment: app connects with Bootstrap Key (raw seed), writes its Device Key public line + newline to stdin; server answers `HERDR-ENROLL:OK:<SHA256:fp>` (appended/authored, bootstrap revoked, exit 0) or typed ERR lines (invalid_key, no_input, expired, unknown_pairing). Then app reconnects with the Device Key. Host persisted only after the full ceremony.\n- App: Device Key = Ed25519 keypair generated on-device, private half stays in Keychain; public half is what a Host authorizes. Pairing uses a dedicated one-shot client beside Transport. Fallbacks: manual Host form + copy-paste authorized_keys line. Risk accepted: same-room attacker photographing the QR and racing within TTL. Reachability scoped to same-LAN/same-VPN; cellular-only phones unsupported.\n\n### 6. libghostty terminal + takeover + SFTP attachments\n- libghostty-spm (ADR-0004): UIKit `UITerminalView` + `InMemoryTerminalSession`; owns parsing, Metal rendering, CoreText, IME, scrollback. Heeler owns keyboards, touch-scroll routing, selection sheet, URL policy, Attach lifecycle. Pinched version; verify SwiftPM checksum before updates. Uses `sendKey` API (libghostty-spm ≥1.6.20260909). ~30 themes, JetBrains Mono & IBM Plex Mono bundled, pinch zoom app-owned.\n- Takeover semantics (ADR-0015): Shell Terminal (Open Terminal) creates a fresh herdr tab via `tab.create` in the Agent's cwd (then worktree path), then attaches the returned root pane's shell through `herdr terminal attach <terminal_id> --takeover` on the existing SSH PTY pipeline. Takeover is safe because the tab is freshly minted; the flow never targets an arbitrary existing terminal (would displace a desktop attach owner). Back detaches, leaving the remote tab alive for desktop handoff. Agent Attach `--takeover` similarly displaces a stale terminal owner. One Host terminal lifetime: opening Shell Terminal tears Agent Attach down first; leaving lets it rejoin.\n- Attachments over SFTP (ADR-0006): Transport.stageImage/stageFile share one SFTP impl (private Host tmp dirs, restrictive perms, partial-file compensation, atomic completion, shared session-channel budget). ≤64 MiB files; images re-encoded metadata-stripped. No PTY binary injection (terminal input has no file framing).\n\n### 7. Worktrees, jump hosts, rough edges\n- Worktrees (CONTEXT.md): a fresh `git checkout` of a workspace's repo created by herdr as its own workspace; branch defaults to herdr's generated `worktree/<name>` off HEAD; removing the Worktree deletes the checkout and closes its workspace but the branch survives. Snapshot worktree metadata describes the main checkout; only `is_linked_worktree` makes a workspace eligible for linked-Worktree removal. New Agent can start in a new Worktree.\n- Jump Hosts (docs/guides/vps-jump-host.md + vps-jump-host-setup.md): reach unroutable Macs behind NAT via a restricted VPS. Mac makes a persistent outbound reverse-SSH tunnel (launchd) publishing a loopback-only port (e.g. 127.0.0.1:2222); iOS connects to the VPS (herdr-jump account, direct-tcpip to 127.0.0.1:2222 only, `AllowTcpForwarding local`, `PermitOpen 127.0.0.1:2222`, `MaxSessions 0`), then does a SECOND SSH handshake to the Mac. Keys verified at both hops; Device Key authorized on both the VPS jump account and the Mac. VPS can observe metadata/interrupt but not passively read the inner session while host keys are verified. No stream-local over the jump; nested driver uses outer direct-tcpip as transport.\n- Rough edges / limitations (documented): requires Node ≥20 + herdr ≥0.7.5 + OpenSSH with stream-local forwarding enabled (onboarding calls out when disabled); advertised SSH port fixed at 22 (plugin README known limitation); herdr API wire shapes carry no stability guarantee (hooks parse leniently); no push-to-start for Live Activities; Live Activity widget shows counts-only on watch/pre-first-unlock; remote history NOT addressable (`pane.read` visible/recent + 1000-line cap, no offset) so no server-side scroll history; shell tabs not projected into Console and outside notification routing; Agent Attach is display-only under Composer (dual-prompt collision); relay is a single point of failure for notifications only (Console/Attach never touch it); App Store availability limited by country; personal-use emphasis 'expect rough edges'. [INFERENCE: no separate 'sync' beyond the sidebar-layout plugin export; no multi-account server.]"
}

