{
  "summary": "Drover is a Flutter (iOS/macOS) app that drives herdr agents over SSH using dartssh2, invoking the herdr CLI per-command (not the socket API). Native transcript history (JSONL) is fetched via SFTP for 5 agents (Claude/Copilot/Codex/Pi/Omp) with a bounded 512KiB window; unmapped agents fall back to pane-text `agent read` output with ANSI stripping. Permission prompts become buttons via a per-agent structured-prompt capability plus a generic numbered-option regex fallback. Push notifications run through Firebase Functions + FCM; a host-side `drover.notify` herdr plugin POSTs `blocked` events (hostId/paneId/eventId) with a paired Bearer credential — payload is plaintext to Google (only credentials hashed), not E2E encrypted. Voice uses on-device speech_to_text; photos are SFTP-uploaded to `<cwd>/.drover` (git-ignored) and referenced by path. Key constraints: herdr version floor 0.8.0, integration must be installed before SessionStart, raw-backtab workaround for mode cycling, notifications only on `blocked` (not `done`).",
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/herdr/herdr_client.dart",
      "description": "HerdrClient over CommandRunner: every herdr CLI call with JSON-envelope error parsing (probes both stdout+stderr, exit-code agnostic); agent list/get/read/prompt/start/rename, pane send-text/send-keys/close/split/list, workspace create/list/close/rename, plugin list/config-dir, herdr --version; SFTP via runner."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/herdr/command_runner.dart",
      "description": "CommandRunner abstraction: run/runWithStdin, uploadFile, listDirectory, resolvePath, statFile, readFile; POSIX shQuote + buildHerdrCommand."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/infra/ssh_command_runner.dart",
      "description": "SshCommandRunner using dartssh2 (SSHSocket.connect + SSHClient, PEM key+passphrase, host-key trust-on-first-use pinning + mismatch detection, 10s auth/exec timeouts, connection invalidation on network change, channel mutex, UTF-8 lossy decode)."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/herdr/host_platform.dart",
      "description": "Host OS detection (uname -s / cmd.exe ver) -> Unix vs WindowsHostPlatform (PowerShell EncodedCommand, UTF-8); transcript-path find/mkdir/prune command assembly."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/herdr/ansi_text.dart",
      "description": "Minimal ANSI SGR parser (fg color + bold, 256/16 palette) -> styled AnsiSpans; stripAnsi."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/herdr/pane_text.dart",
      "description": "stripTuiChrome (removes box-drawing rules, -- INSERT --, status/mode glyph lines, empty prompts) + parsePromptOptions generic numbered-option permission prompt fallback (regex ^(\\s*)(❯\\s*)?(\\d+)\\.\\s+, needs >=2 consecutive options)."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/transcript/native_transcript.dart",
      "description": "Native transcript model (Message/ToolUse/Thinking/ToolResult), StructuredPrompt model, toolUseSummary, JsonlTranscriptWindow (bounded 512KiB tail, append-only polling, pull-to-load-more older chunks, truncation reset)."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/agents/agent_registry.dart",
      "description": "Compile-time registry: Claude, Copilot, Codex, Pi, Omp adapters (the native-transcript agents)."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/agents/agent_adapter.dart",
      "description": "AgentAdapter capability contract: native history, mode cycling, structured prompts, image attachments; generic fallbacks when a capability is null."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/agents/agent_native_history.dart",
      "description": "NativeTranscriptHistory: resolves adapter per agent_session identity, serializes loads, caches latest snapshot."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/agents/structured_prompt_helpers.dart",
      "description": "findLastUnansweredToolUse (pending structured prompt by unanswered tool_use id), normalizePaneText, pollUntil (read-driven key injection)."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/agents/agent_image_upload.dart",
      "description": "Upload images via SFTP to <cwd>/.drover/img-<ts>-<i>.<ext>, writes .gitignore '*', prunes >2 days; path-reference syntax is agent-specific."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/image/image_input.dart",
      "description": "ImagePickerPort via image_picker (gallery multi / camera iOS-only); extension sanitized to [a-z0-9]."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/lib/src/speech/speech_input.dart",
      "description": "SpeechInput via speech_to_text: on-device dictation only, partialResults, autoPunctuation, ja_JP default; on-device support probed via platform channel."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/herdr-notes.md",
      "description": "Herdr CLI behaviors/gotchas: version floor, agent prompt, integration-hook gating of agent_session, shift+tab backtab bug, text-only input channel + SFTP path, error-channel inconsistency, terminal_title_stripped."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/agents/claude-notes.md",
      "description": "Claude specifics: raw-backtab mode-cycle order, bare-path image input, AskUserQuestion TUI answering by key injection, ~/.claude/projects JSONL layout."
    },
    {
      "path": "functions/src/index.ts",
      "description": "Firebase Functions backend: registerDevice/unregisterDevice/sendTestNotification/createPairingCode/revokeHost (onCall, App Check) + completePairing/sendBlockedNotification (onRequest); credentials+pairing codes stored only as SHA-256 hashes; event dedup 24h; FCM multicast."
    },
    {
      "path": "functions/src/validation.ts",
      "description": "Payload validation: deviceId/pairingCode/paneId patterns, BlockedNotification shape, notificationContent, sanitizeSingleLine."
    },
    {
      "path": "keinstn/drover-notify (herdr-plugin.toml, src/event.mjs, src/notification-client.mjs, bin/handle-blocked.mjs)",
      "description": "drover.notify herdr plugin: subscribes pane.agent_status_changed, sends ONLY blocked, POSTs hostId/paneId/eventId(UUID)/agentName with Bearer credential to sendBlockedNotification; zero npm deps."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/push-notifications.md",
      "description": "Pairing flow: manual plugin install/link, pairing code via app, host writes credential to config.json (0600), notification data + hostId validation on tap."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/firebase-setup.md",
      "description": "Firebase product setup, App Check (App Attest iOS release), Firestore TTL for events/pairingCodes."
    }
  ],
  "architecture": "Flutter app <--(SSH, dartssh2, key auth)--> herdr host running the herdr CLI (driven per-command, JSON envelopes) + herdr integration hooks + the drover.notify plugin. Two data channels: (1) host->app polling/commands over SSH exec + SFTP file transfers; (2) asynchronous notifications: drover.notify on the host POSTs 'blocked' events over HTTPS to Firebase Functions (Bearer host credential), which relays via FCM to the device; the device itself only registers an FCM token and creates pairing codes. The app foreground-polls agent list and reads transcripts either natively (JSONL over SFTP, bounded windows) or from `agent read --source recent --format ansi`. AgentKind -> AgentAdapter registry selects per-agent capabilities (native history, mode cycling via raw backtab ESC[Z, structured-prompt answering by key injection, image path referencing).",
  "report": "DROVER INTERNALS (keinstn/drover, MIT; Flutter app + Firebase Functions backend). drover-notify plugin is a separate repo (keinstn/drover-notify).\n\n1) TRANSPORT / CLI vs SOCKET — SSH via dartssh2 (pubspec: dartssh2 ^4.1.0). It drives the herdr CLI over SSH, NOT a direct socket API (spike.dart + SshCommandRunner run `herdr <args>` in one exec each, serialized on a mutex, one channel at a time). infra/ssh_command_runner.dart: SSHSocket.connect + SSHClient, private key from PEM + optional passphrase (SSHKeyPair.fromPem), host-key trust-on-first-use with fingerprint pinning and SshHostKeyMismatchException, 10s auth + exec timeout bounds, drops a wedged client on SSHChannelOpenError/Timeout, connection invalidation on network change, mutex-serialized channel use, UTF-8 lossy decode. Host OS auto-detected (uname -s / cmd.exe ver); WindowsHostPlatform assembles PowerShell -EncodedCommand lines (forces UTF-8, exits with $LASTEXITCODE). Commands (herdr_client.dart): agent list/get/read --source recent --format ansi/prompt/start --kind --pane/rename; pane send-text/send-keys/close/split/list; workspace create --no-focus/list/close/rename; plugin list --plugin <id> --json; plugin config-dir; herdr --version. Errors parsed from JSON envelope {error:{code,message}} on BOTH channels regardless of exit code. SFTP (dartssh2 SftpClient) used for uploadFile/readFile/statFile/listDirectory/resolvePath (images and native transcript files).\n\n2) TRANSCRIPT HISTORY + RENDERING — Two sources. (a) NATIVE via `agent_session` (present only when a herdr integration hook is installed: herdr integration install claude/codex/copilot/pi/omp; only from the NEXT SessionStart). Adapters: Claude, Copilot, Codex, Pi, Omp (agent_registry.dart). JSONL files located on host (Claude under ~/.claude/projects, found by session id) and read over SFTP via JsonlTranscriptWindow: bounded 512KiB tail window initial load, append-only polling (only bytes past known EOF), pull-to-load-more paging older chunks, truncation/replaced-file reset, oversized-record skip. Parsed to TranscriptMessage / TranscriptToolUse / TranscriptThinking / TranscriptToolResult. (b) PANE-TEXT FALLBACK for unmapped agents: `agent read --source recent --format ansi` (bounded by herdr's retained pane buffer). ansi_text.dart parses SGR escapes into styled runs; pane_text.dart stripTuiChrome() strips box-drawing rules (─), `-- INSERT --` mode lines, status/mode glyph lines, empty `❯` prompts. Turn markers per herdr-notes Measurements: `❯` user, `⏺` assistant/action, `✻ Worked for Ns` meta footer; trailing `-- INSERT --` mode line stripped. Session title from herdr `terminal_title_stripped` (drops one leading spinner glyph) + client-side suffix strip (e.g. ' - GitHub Copilot').\n\n3) PERMISSION PROMPTS -> BUTTONS — (a) Structured-prompt capability per agent from native JSONL (Claude AskUserQuestion tool_use: input.questions[]{question,header,multiSelect,options[]}; 'pending' = last unanswered tool_use via findLastUnansweredToolUse). Answered by injecting keys through the TUI: option digits / custom text via `pane send-text`, Enter/arrows via `pane send-keys`; READ-DRIVEN injector (re-reads pane after each keystroke, aborts on unknown state; dialog detected by 'Esc to cancel' footer; multi-select: digits toggle then right -> Submit '1. Submit answers'). (b) GENERIC FALLBACK: parsePromptOptions() scans last 30 lines for numbered-option prompt via regex `^(\\s*)(❯\\s*)?(\\d+)\\.\\s+(\\S.*)$`, requires >=2 options numbered 1..N consecutively, marks selected (❯), derives question from preceding line ending '?'; tapping types that digit.\n\n4) NOTIFICATIONS — Firebase backend (functions/). What leaves the DEVICE: FCM token + deviceId + platform + notifyOnBlocked/notifyOnDone, registered under Firebase Auth anonymous uid (registerDevice onCall, App Check App Attest iOS); createPairingCode(hostId) -> pairing code. The EVENT payload leaves the HOST, not the device: the drover.notify herdr plugin POSTs ONLY `blocked` to the Functions HTTP endpoint sendBlockedNotification, body {hostId, paneId, eventId(UUID), agentName?, status}, header Authorization: Bearer <host credential>. Relay: pairing code (randomBytes(32) base64url) and host credential (randomBytes(32) base64url) are stored/checked ONLY as SHA-256 hashes (pairingCode doc id = sha256; credentialHash via timingSafeEqual); completePairing exchanges a one-time 10-min code for credential + notificationUrl; sendBlockedNotification authorizes, dedupes by eventId (Firestore events collection, 24h TTL), then FCM multicast-delivers (title 'Agent needs your input' / 'Agent finished'). Device on receipt validates hostId against saved config and opens the pane on tap. E2E encryption: NO. {hostId,paneId,eventId,agentName} travel in plaintext (TLS in transit, visible to the Firebase project); only credentials/pairing codes are hashed. Schema supports 'done'/notifyOnDone but the shipped plugin only sends blocked.\n\n5) VOICE + PHOTO — Voice: speech_to_text ^7.4.0, ON-DEVICE dictation only (ListenMode.dictation, partialResults, autoPunctuation, cancelOnError, onDevice:true; ja_JP for ja); capability probed via platform channel com.keinstn.drover/speech 'supportsOnDeviceRecognition'; one shared SpeechInputController (plugin singleton). Photo: image_picker ^1.2.3 (gallery single/multi; camera iOS-only); read bytes + sanitized extension ([a-z0-9], fallback png); uploaded via SFTP to `<cwd>/.drover/img-<ts>-<i>.<ext>`, writes .gitignore '*', prunes img-* >2 days; referenced from an ordinary text prompt as a bare absolute path (Claude) or @mention (Copilot) — agent-specific; staying under cwd avoids out-of-workspace read permission prompts.\n\n6) LIMITATIONS / ROUGH EDGES — herdr version floor 0.8.0 enforced per host (persistent warning + blocks launches below; agent prompt/start --pane/wait --until require it); herdr-api-snapshot unreleased (uses agent list); integration must be installed BEFORE SessionStart or native history silently falls back to pane-text (bounded buffer; install doesn't affect running agents); a send right after agent start can be silently dropped (confirm by re-polling); agent start without explicit --workspace hijacks the focused workspace (closing it kills the agent); mode cycling needs raw-backtab workaround ESC[Z via pane send-text (pane send-keys shift+tab broken up to herdr 0.8.0/0.8.2 — writes a plain Tab byte, fails silently); input channel is text-only, no synthetic image paste (SFTP+path); herdr plugin install clones over unauthenticated HTTPS (can't fetch private repos; use git clone + herdr plugin link); error envelope channel/exit code inconsistent (must probe both stdout+stderr); agent `name` is a slug not a display title (uses terminal_title_stripped); Windows admin hosts need public key in C:\\ProgramData\\ssh\\administrators_authorized_keys; pairing config.json holds the host credential (don't copy/commit); notifications only on blocked (no done in practice); App Check only on iOS Release; on-device speech required (no network STT); free Apple ID signing expires after 7 days.\n\nHOST REQUIREMENTS — SSH with key-based auth; herdr >=0.8.0; one herdr integration per agent for native transcripts; Node >=18 for the drover.notify plugin (zero npm deps)."
}

